ptember 30, 1987","quote_kind":"verbatim_note_item","quote_truncated":false,"status":"CANDIDATE_UNVERIFIED"},"proposal":{"actor":"EO:12610","date":"1987-09-30","mechanism":"revocation","source":{"page_or_item":"OFR API record executive_order_number=12511; citation 50 FR 18449; field disposition_notes","sha256":"8ba9e1cce593bb06b6be625b585b15bb04a1555ed34ad8c5b6f8c9bd81f83f77","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents?conditions%5Bcorrection%5D=0&conditions%5Bpresidential_document_type%5D=executive_order&conditions%5Btype%5D%5B%5D=PRESDOCU&fields%5B%5D=citation&fields%5B%5D=disposition_notes&fields%5B%5D=document_number&fields%5B%5D=executive_order_number&fields%5B%5D=html_url&fields%5B%5D=pdf_url&fields%5B%5D=president&fields%5B%5D=publication_date&fields%5B%5D=raw_text_url&fields%5B%5D=signing_date&fields%5B%5D=title&format=json&include_pre_1994_docs=true&order=executive_order_number&page=6&per_page=1000&search_after_cursor=WzEyNDk3LjAsIjEyNDk3Il0"}},"suggested":true}],"whole_order_end_total":1},"provisional_status":"no","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"confirm","counterevidence":"confirm","ending_or_current_basis":"confirm","opus_media":"n/a","original_text":"confirm","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":[],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1985-04-29","later-events_catalog":"1985-04-29","stage19_causal_queue":"1985-04-29"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:12511","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) There is established the President’s Child Safety  \nPartnership.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"50 FR 18449, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"8231b1df1807fa64869516db2a86780d29e4619f26763b61434763a267db5eff","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1985-05-01/pdf/FR-1985-05-01.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12511#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Partnership shall be composed of not more than 26 members designat­\ned or appointed by the President from among citizens of the United States, and  \nshall include the Attorney General, the Secretary of Health and Human  \nServices, and the Secretary of Education. The President shall designate a  \nChairman from among the members of the Partnership.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"50 FR 18449, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"8231b1df1807fa64869516db2a86780d29e4619f26763b61434763a267db5eff","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1985-05-01/pdf/FR-1985-05-01.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12511#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Partnership shall exam ine issues and make recom ­\nmendations to the President on preventing the victimization and promoting the  \nsafety of children in the United States.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"50 FR 18449, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"8231b1df1807fa64869516db2a86780d29e4619f26763b61434763a267db5eff","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1985-05-01/pdf/FR-1985-05-01.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12511#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Partnership m ay conduct such studies, inquiries, hearings, and m eet­\nings as m ay be n ecessary to carry out its functions. The focus of the Partner­\nship’s inquiries and reports shall be on recommendations for public-private  \ncooperation to encourage and facilitate private sector involvement in child  \nsafety efforts, including activities appropriate for action by service organiza­\ntions, schools, businesses, charitable organizations, and public safety organi­\nzations.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"50 FR 18449, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"8231b1df1807fa64869516db2a86780d29e4619f26763b61434763a267db5eff","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1985-05-01/pdf/FR-1985-05-01.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12511#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Partnership shall report to the President from time to time as requested  \nand shall submit its final report by April 29,1987.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"50 FR 18449, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 2(c)","sha256":"8231b1df1807fa64869516db2a86780d29e4619f26763b61434763a267db5eff","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1985-05-01/pdf/FR-1985-05-01.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12511#sec2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The heads of Executive agencies shall, to -the extent  \npermitted by law, provide the Partnership such information as it may require  \nto carry out its functions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"50 FR 18449, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"8231b1df1807fa64869516db2a86780d29e4619f26763b61434763a267db5eff","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1985-05-01/pdf/FR-1985-05-01.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12511#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Members of the Partnership shall serve without compensation for their  \nwork on the Partnership. However, members appointed from among private  \ncitizens, including employees from State and local government, may, subject  \nto the availability of funds, be allowed travel expenses, including per diem in  \nlieu of subsistence, as authorized by law»for persons serving intermittently in  \nthe government service (5 U.S.C. 5701-5707).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"50 FR 18449, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"8231b1df1807fa64869516db2a86780d29e4619f26763b61434763a267db5eff","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1985-05-01/pdf/FR-1985-05-01.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12511#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Attorney General shall, to the extent permitted by law, provide the  \nPartnership with such administrative services, funds, facilities, staff, and other  \nsupport services as may be necessary for the performance of its functions.\nSeci 4. G eneral, (a) The Departments of Justice, Health and Human Services,  \nand Education are directed to join with the Partnership to encourage the  \ndevelopment of public/private sector initiatives to prevent and respond to the  \nvictimization of children.\n(b) Notwithstanding any other Executive order, the functions of the President  \nunder the Federal Advisory Committee Act, as amended, except that of  \nreporting to the Congress, which are applicable to the Partnership, shall be  \nperformed by the Attorney General, in accordance with guidelines and proce­\ndures established by the Administrator of General Services.\n\n=== PDF page 14 of 194 ===\n18450 Federal Register /  Voi. 50, No. 84 / W ednesday, May 1, 1985 /  Presidental Documents\n(c } The Partnership shall terminate on April 29, 1987, or 60 days after submit­\nting its final report, whichever is earlier.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"50 FR 18449, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"8231b1df1807fa64869516db2a86780d29e4619f26763b61434763a267db5eff","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1985-05-01/pdf/FR-1985-05-01.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12511#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"50 FR 18449, PDF pages 13-14","sha256":"8231b1df1807fa64869516db2a86780d29e4619f26763b61434763a267db5eff","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1985-05-01/pdf/FR-1985-05-01.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 8 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:12511"}
